         "## Why a public map",
         "Potholes are a constant source of anger in Indian cities during and after the monsoon, when heavy rain breaks up road surfaces. In Pune, residents filed more than 14,000 pothole complaints between June and September last year.",
         "“Before, you complained and never heard anything,” said a software engineer in Kothrud who has reported 23 potholes this year. “Now I can see the ward officer's name and how many days it has been open.”",
         "## Contractors named",
         "Roads repaired under warranty must be fixed by the original contractor at no cost to the city. The map shows which roads are still under warranty, so residents and councillors can see when the same contractor's work keeps failing.",
